## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to translate graph-based access policy constraints into a three-valued logical solver while managing constraint satisfaction risks. The directed graph structure introduces transitive reasoning requirements, making the problem more realistic than handling independent logical clauses.

## Key Concepts
- Three-valued logic propagation using Kleene semantics (T > U > F)
- Arc-consistency enforcement on directed constraint graphs
- Not-both-true constraint handling and conflict detection
- Backtracking strategies for partial truth assignments

## Code Example
```javascript
function propagate(vals, edges) {
  // vals: {N1:'T'|'F'|'U',...}
  // edges: [[from, to], ...]
  let changed = true;
  while (changed) {
    changed = false;
    for (const [from, to] of edges) {
      if (vals[from] === 'T' && vals[to] === 'F') {
        return false; // Constraint violated
      }
      if (vals[from] === 'T' && vals[to] === 'U') {
        vals[to] = 'T';
        changed = true;
      }
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests design of a constraint solver for non-classical logics with custom operators and propagation strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued semantics (T > U > F)
- Custom operators →* (strong implication) and ⊕ (parity)
- Forward checking, variable ordering, and backtracking in non-deterministic domains

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Kleene 3-valued semantics (T=1, U=0, F=-1)
const T=1, U=0, F=-1;
function not(v){ return v===T?F : v===F?T : U; }
function kleeneAnd(a,b){ if(a===F||b===F) return F; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return T; }
function kleeneOr(a,b){ if(a===T||b===T) return T; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return F; }
function strongImpl(a,b){ // placeholder behavior for demonstration
  if(a===F) return T; if(a===T) return b; return (b===F?F:(b===U?U:T));
}
function parity(a,b){ // placeholder: U propagates unless forced by T/F
  if(a===F||b===F) return F; if(a===T&&b===T) return T; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return F;
}
```

